      "math_academy_id": "q-225087",
      "sequence_position": 5,
      "problem": "Using the cumulative distribution function table of the Poisson random variable $X∼\\text{Po}(3.6)$ given below, compute $P(X\\ge 5).$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ | $6$ | $7$ | $8$ | $9$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $P(X\\le x)$ | $\\,0.5152\\,$ | $\\,0.7064\\,$ | $\\,0.8441\\,$ | $\\,0.9267\\,$ | $\\,0.9692\\,$ | $\\,0.9883\\,$ | $\\,0.9960\\,$ |\n\n$P(X\\ge 5)=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "The cumulative distribution function of a discrete random variable $X$ is a function $F(x)$ such that\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x).\n$$\n\nTo solve the given problem, we can use the rule\n\n$$\nP(X>a)=1-P(X\\le a)=1-F(a).\n$$\n\nNow, note that \n\n$$\nP(X\\ge 5)=P(X>4).\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 5) & =P(X>4) \\\\  & =1-P(X\\le 4) \\\\  & =1-F(4) \\\\  & =1-0.7064 \\\\  & =0.2936.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
